# Host values: text that identifies a host.
#
# scripts/scan.sh reports each line that contains one of these patterns.
# A finding fails on the branch portable, on a tag portable-v* and in an
# image; it is a warning on other branches (docs/secret-handling.md).
#
# This file is tracked and holds no pattern: a pattern of a real host would
# put that host value into the tree that it forbids. The patterns of a host
# go into the untracked file .local/host-values.deny (same format). The scan
# reads it when it exists. scripts/host-values.regex gives the generic rules.
#
# Format: one literal pattern for each line, case-insensitive. A line that
# starts with "#" is a comment. Quotes and backslashes are not allowed.
# The scan does not report host values in this file and in
# .local/host-values.deny.
